(
 '* 0.19.0 ⋄ 2026-09-19'
 '  * Requires Dyalog 18.2 or better now (was 18.0)'
 '  * ]ReportAllIssues accepts -filename= now, as its help always claimed'
 '  * ]ListRepos honours -sort=issues without -verbose; -issues defaults to that order now'
 '  * The API is documented in the ReadMe now'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * ]ListIssues -html -verbose produced no HTML at all'
 '    * ]ReportAllIssues omitted repos with just one or two open issues'
 '    * ]ReportAllIssues -? printed nothing'
 '    * ]GoToGitHub created an invalid URL when the owner''s home page was selected'
 '    * The first call after a cold start did nothing but load the dependencies'
 '    * Assert ignored an error number passed as part of its right argument'
 '* 0.18.0 ⋄ 2026-07-19'
 '  * Packages updated (MarkAPL)'
 '* 0.17.0 ⋄ 2026-07-06'
 '  * User command ]ReportAllIssues added'
 '  * ]ListIssues has a new option: -assignees='
 '  * README polished'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '  * User command help (-??) transformed into variables (much easier to edit)'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * ]ListIssues did not process assignee correctly'
 '* 0.16.0 ⋄ 2025-09-21'
 '  * Syntax of ]GoToGitHub has changed'
 '* 0.15.0 ⋄ 2025-04-23'
 '  * `ListRepos` now honours a flag `issues`'
 '  * `ListRepos` now allows to specify the desired sort order with -sort=[name | issues]'
 '  * Allows the specification of an access token now, either via the config file or as environment variables'
 '  * `Version` returns the version number from the package config file as a char vector'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '* 0.14.0 ⋄ 2024-09-08'
 '  * Syntax of GoToGitHub vastly extended'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * `ListIssues` could be called with no argument; that made no sense '
 '* 0.13.0 ⋄ 2024-08-05'
 '  `GoToGitHub` added '
 '* 0.12.0 ⋄ 2024-06-18'
)
